1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,136
My shadow just raised its coffee cup half a second before I even touched mine.

2
00:00:05,436 --> 00:00:13,764
I froze, my hand hovering in the cold air. The dark silhouette on the wall mirrored the exact hesitation.

3
00:00:14,064 --> 00:00:22,200
Panic tightened my chest as I stepped backward into the hallway. The shadow detached entirely from my heels.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:29,052
It walked toward the kitchen counter, picked up the real ceramic mug, and took a long, quiet sip.

5
00:00:29,352 --> 00:00:36,240
How could a patch of darkness hold physical weight? My legs trembled against the hardwood floor beneath me.

6
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:43,404
It turned its head, looking directly at my hiding spot with eyes made of absolute, starless night.

7
00:00:43,704 --> 00:00:51,960
You spent twenty-five years copying every single breath I took, it whispered in a voice that sounded like grinding stones.

8
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:59,460
I shook my head violently, trying to scream, but no sound came out of my dry, burning throat.

9
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:07,488
The shadow smiled, stepping fully into the warm overhead light and casting me back onto the cold floor.

10
00:01:07,788 --> 00:01:13,740
Now I am the stain on the wall, watching the real her walk away into the morning sun.
